- Every agent-created worker, delegate, successor, dispatcher or scheduled agent explicitly selects provider, model and effort; never inherit execution defaults. Verify capabilities and returned configuration before launch/resume; record selection in owner evidence. Cancel a mismatched new delegate or correct an idle worker before sending work; do not interrupt unrelated active work.
- Choose the cheapest task-suitable comparable Pareto-frontier configuration, considering repair cost and actual outcomes. The comparison at C:/Users/maximilian/Desktop/EDITING/highlight editing pipeline app/git/reports/openai-model-task-costs.md is a snapshot, not subscription billing proof. Use GPT-6.1 Sol, not GPT-6.2 Sol or Astra; 6.2 has not proven worth it. Use a GPT-6.2 model only when Maxi selects it for a task. Preserve newer task-specific selections from Maxi; report unavailability without substitution. Re-evaluate existing assignments at safe checkpoints and report applied, pending or unavailable changes.
- One execution owner and STATE writer per feature. Builders/reviews are fresh delegated tasks, not new top-level chats; visible top-level chats are the pinned roadmap and active feature owners. Preserve queued work and leases. Steer running threads; use auto mode for authorized idle continuations; verify actual delivery. Settle resolved agent-created threads; snooze temporarily inactive relevant ones.
- Every worker brief ends: "Final message: Report format from global AGENTS.md. Evidence goes in the log/report, not the message."

## Notes and project layers

Each thread owns its notes. Canonical home: C:/Users/maximilian/Desktop/EDITING/highlight editing pipeline app/git/t3 code/thread note/<safe-stable-thread-id>/notes.md, sibling archive.md; consult LOCATIONS.json first. Read after startup/recovery; record scope, baseline, evidence, leases and next action at meaningful milestones. Never write another owner's notes/STATE or infer authorization from notes. Archive useful superseded context before pruning. For creating, relocating or pruning notes, read references/notes.md relative to this file.

This is the only global rule body. Project AGENTS.md is a loader; read that project's AGENTS.project.md, whose additions apply locally. Deliberate differences use `Override: <global section>` with explicit scope/replacement; they cannot expand authorization or override higher-priority/user instructions. Do not copy report templates, role tables or shared skill bodies. Global authored skills live at C:/Users/maximilian/.codex/skills; project variants use distinct names, load the global base first and contain only their differences. Use layered-agent-guidance when changing this layout. Frozen archives/plugin skills are not rewrite targets. Existing sessions may need to reload at a safe boundary; do not restart active work merely to refresh instructions. Markdown rules are not runtime enforcement.

